      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_7f528559ecd2919a896cb7b48af3b00ba54a5a24735fa4371bd87e0268208d03",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Under their respective dilation conventions, both sources expose finite resolution of the fractional-part dictionary. The deterministic criterion restricts an exact Nyman-Beurling equivalence to an arithmetic sequence of dilations. In the random criterion, conditioning on all dilations being admissible lets the deterministic distance bound be evaluated at the random minimum m_n, producing the lower bound D_n^2 much greater than 1/(log 2+E|log m_n|).",
