    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_85019103bf1b3499a8316703b7b2716b38d1dcb36ea66b341aaf407d6d785d37",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The candidate groups several unrelated uses of functional equations or completion: modular and spectral symmetries of an Eisenstein series, an unconditional reflected-zeta quotient bound used after an RH-dependent construction, a remote-contour sign argument for an extended-Selberg-class function, and computational nonconfirmation for Hurwitz and Lerch cases. The parents do not supply a shared criterion, representation map, or theorem connecting these modules.",
