    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_e5ed9b5d3fb68b3d05a03c24214c0d1f873ef6d60f12c1801b8ec2657313688d",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The survey's Nyman-Beurling closure equivalence is resolved locally by the detailed proof: at a hypothetical zeta zero with 1/2<Re(s)<1, Mellin evaluation annihilates every fractional-part generator through its zeta factor but gives the indicator target the nonzero value 1/s. Splitting the error at t=1 makes this evaluation continuous along the approximating sequence and yields a contradiction.",
