    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_f96cdfc2a3ac0b03b54b07ebb7075183b2e30b9d3e89bb2733fccd16fa1f2f0d",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Lagarias's all-integer inequality is equivalent to RH because its harmonic expression is a rate-compatible two-sided envelope around Robin's benchmark e^gamma n log log n. Under RH, Robin's universal bound handles n>=5041 and a reported finite computation handles the prefix. Under RH failure, Robin's infinitely-often excess of order n log log n/(log n)^beta with beta<1/2 eventually exceeds the harmonic envelope's O(n/log n) slack.",
